Description: Reset the size of a container promoted by a directional move
 When a directional move promotes a tiled container out of its parent
 (for example W in H[X Y H[A W]] moved right), sway kept the container's
 old size fraction, which was relative to its former parent, and reset
 the fraction of the ancestor it left. The promoted container then got
 an oversized share and its neighbours shrank. i3 resets the moved
 container instead, as sway already does on its other reparenting paths.
 .
 Taken from the open upstream pull request, carried until it is merged.
 Applied on top of 12-i3-tree-moves.patch: the reset goes after the focus
 order update that patch adds, before the container is inserted.
Author: Pablo <pablocpascual@gmail.com>
Origin: https://github.com/swaywm/sway/pull/9249 (commit e3139d49ad62e07d0962fdae6d881b3914b17d30)
Bug: https://github.com/swaywm/sway/issues/9248
Forwarded: not-needed
Applied-Upstream: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-11
---
--- a/sway/commands/move.c
+++ b/sway/commands/move.c
@@ -486,6 +486,9 @@ static bool container_move_in_direction(
 		struct sway_container *old_parent = container->pending.parent;
 		focus_order_for_insert(container, node_get_parent(&ancestor->node),
 				&ancestor->node);
+		// The container's fractions were relative to its former parent.
+		container->pending.height = container->pending.width = 0;
+		container->height_fraction = container->width_fraction = 0;
 		if (ancestor->pending.parent) {
 			// Container will move in with its parent
 			container_insert_child(ancestor->pending.parent, container,
@@ -496,8 +499,8 @@ static bool container_move_in_direction(
 			workspace_insert_tiling(ancestor->pending.workspace, container,
 					index + (offs < 0 ? 0 : 1));
 		}
+		// The ancestor remains in the same parent, so preserve its fractions.
 		ancestor->pending.height = ancestor->pending.width = 0;
-		ancestor->height_fraction = ancestor->width_fraction = 0;
 		if (old_parent) {
 			container_reap_empty(old_parent);
 		}
